+## What would advance the case
+
+1. **Equipment and authority.** Find the actual 2000–2002 ACO-400 and M-70 submissions and enclosures, applicable WOCC/endpoint determinations and reviews, and line installation and acceptance records. Cross-check the line identifier, effective dates and change history against the OIG's account. This test is unperformed.
+2. **Regulatory transition and custody.** Find DOT 1600.17B, the basis and record of any FAA revalidation of 1600.24D, any intervening instructions and the transfer or retention documentation for each inventory series. The catalog office fields alone leave inventory custody open.
+3. **Preservation and correction.** Seek the final recommendation 3 response, issued retention policy and implementation/closure evidence. Retain the actual corrected May 2003 answer and delivery acknowledgment, signed consideration/action/no-action decision and recommendation-specific dispositions as independent, higher-priority targets.
+
+Scope was the referenced text and selected page images. The six saved source and comparison bodies were hashed and exact locators checked. The indexed catalog extract is a separate, unhashed observation. The page image and text extraction values remain separate. Device listings, where obtained, can establish reported equipment coverage. Call-specific logs and recordings would be needed to establish that an individual call was recorded. The work-plan dependencies remain open. [Source pins](SOURCE-PINS.json) · [Additive text diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff)
